{"message":"Your identity is verified, and I logged the verification. I checked your Green and Blue accounts and their debit cards: both accounts are open, both cards are active, and neither shows an active fraud alert or temporary velocity block. Your available account holdings are sufficient for a normal cash withdrawal, so the three declines do not appear to be caused by your Green or Blue account status.

Because all three cards declined at the same ATM, please use a different nearby ATM—preferably a Rho-Bank or partner ATM—and avoid repeated attempts at the current machine. If the ATM displayed a decline code, please send me the exact code/message. That will let me determine whether this is a terminal issue, a withdrawal-limit issue, or another restriction.

The teen card may have separate parental controls or a $150 daily ATM limit. I can’t inspect your daughter’s card details without verifying the teen account holder or confirming the appropriate authorized access."}
